---
import { withBase } from "../lib/base.js";
---

<section id="origin" class="section origin">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="section-tag">Meet the leaves</span>
    <div class="section-heading">
      <h2>Why our matcha slaps</h2>
      <p>
        We didn't just grab the first tin of green powder we saw. Moof works with two exclusive
        Japanese matchas &mdash; Mori and Shiran &mdash; picked for very specific vibes.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="origin-grid">
      <div class="origin-card">
        <span class="badge badge-pink origin-stamp">Japan 🇯🇵</span>
        <p class="origin-name"><span class="origin-flag">🍵</span> Mori</p>
        <p class="origin-tagline">deep, rounded, does not play around</p>
        <p class="origin-body">
          Mori goes deep green with a rounded, full-bodied finish. It's the one we reach for when a
          drink needs richness and body &mdash; think our Specialty Matcha Latte and Usucha, where
          the matcha has nowhere to hide and doesn't need to.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="origin-card">
        <span class="badge badge-sky origin-stamp">Japan 🇯🇵</span>
        <p class="origin-name"><span class="origin-flag">🍃</span> Shiran</p>
        <p class="origin-tagline">smooth, clean, plays well with milk</p>
        <p class="origin-body">
          Shiran is the smoother-profile matcha &mdash; bright, clean, and built for layered milk
          teas. It's what gives our Classic Matcha Latte that soft, no-bitterness-here finish
          people keep coming back for.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="origin-note">
      <span>🫡</span>
      <span>
        Every drink is hand-whisked to order &mdash; ceremonial-grade matcha, actual technique, zero
        shortcuts. Your barista is basically doing a tiny tea ceremony for you.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
